libGLcompat provides the OpenGL entry points that IRIX's <GL/gl.h>
declares but IRIX 6.5's libGL.so and libGLcore.so do not export:
OpenGL 1.3 and 1.4 (glActiveTexture, glMultiTexCoord*,
glCompressedTexImage*, glWindowPos*, ...) and the ARB, EXT, ATI and NV
extensions of SGI's later systems. Programs that call them then link.

Each function calls the driver's own implementation when
glXGetProcAddressARB finds one, under its name or its core or ARB/EXT
twin, and otherwise does nothing (programs check the extension string
or version first). pkgsrc links it after libGL on IRIX, so a libGL that
exports a function itself still provides it.

lib/pkgconfig/gl.pc is for programs built outside pkgsrc: pkg-config
--libs gl gives IRIX's libGL and libGLcore by path, then libGLcompat.
(-lGL with -L/usr/pkg/lib would link lib/libGL.so, the run-time shim
that makes IRIX's libGL work with pkgsrc's X11.)
